# Written by the framework and the tooling, and regenerated by the next build or
# dev run: formatting them changes nothing that survives, and rewriting `dist`
# would reformat minified bundles and built HTML for no reason.
#
# A package-level `prettier --write .` does not read the repository root's ignore
# file, so this has to exist here as well for `pnpm -r format` to be safe.
.astro/
.wrangler/
dist/

# Lockfiles are pnpm's to write, wherever they are — the same reason the root
# ignore file lists the root one. (This nested copy should probably not exist at
# all: a pnpm workspace has one lockfile, and this one predates the workspace.)
pnpm-lock.yaml
